==Strategy==
Two Attack Up [[Cat Combo|Combos]] (such as [[Brave Cutter (Combo)|Brave Cutter]] & [[Tiny Ancient Hunt (Combo)|Tiny Ancient Hunt]],) [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]], [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]], [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Ectoweight Cat]], a fast rusher cat of your choice (such as [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] or [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]), an area attacker ([[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] works well) and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]].

This stage features a long-distance boss with some medium-strength support. Do not bring any slow cats (like Pizza Cat and Cameraman Cat) as they're just going to get knocked back by Dead Donny Dash over and over again. Housewife can be a little hit or miss, as it narrowly fits into Donny Dash's blind spot, so any anti-zombie ubers will work great here as always. Stall in the beginning and spam your attackers when the boss comes out. The support can be overwhelming if it doesn't die more or less before the Donny Dash un-burrows, so make sure to get it out of the way with the area attacker. Spawn Awakened Bahamut when there's not much in the way, and he should be able to quickly destroy the boss and the base.

